# hlsdemux creates an output stream for every rendition of the selected variant except
# SUBTITLES: setup_streams passes `selected` as VIDEO || AUDIO and create_stream_for_playlist
# returns without creating anything for a stream that is not selected, so a master playlist
# whose subtitles live in their own EXT-X-MEDIA rendition exposes no text stream at all.
#
# Selecting the rendition is only half of it. A WebVTT fragment carries its cue times on its
# own timeline and ties that timeline to the presentation with an X-TIMESTAMP-MAP header, so
# the cue times have to be converted before they mean anything to a player. The successor
# element does that in ext/adaptivedemux2/hls/gsthlsdemux-util.c against a map of internal
# (MPEG-TS) time to stream time; this carries that conversion over, taking the map from the
# primary stream's first PCR and the stream time of the fragment it came from -- both of
# which this element already computes. Where the successor's fallbacks apply they are kept
# verbatim: a fragment with no X-TIMESTAMP-MAP is read as carrying MPEG-TS values, a cue that
# cannot be converted because no primary fragment has provided a PCR yet keeps its original
# value, and a cue that converts to a negative stream time is clamped to zero.
#
# A rendition's NAME and LANGUAGE become its stream's title and language tags. They are kept
# on the stream and merged into every tag event it sends, because the element sends other tags
# on the same stream -- the ID3 tags of a packed audio fragment, a bitrate change -- and a new
# stream tag event replaces the one before it downstream.
#
# A rendition's CHARACTERISTICS travel with them, as the string tag "hls-characteristics" the
# element registers. The rendition's stream also carries its tags, type and flags in a GstStream
# on its stream-start event, so a player finds them when it first sees the stream rather than
# whenever the tag events arrive. A URI rendition's tags additionally go out in the typed
# "hls-rendition-tags" event described below, so a demuxer splitting its fragments applies them
# over the container's own values, as hlsdemux2 applies a rendition's LANGUAGE with
# GST_TAG_MERGE_REPLACE over the demuxed tags.
#
# A rendition without a URI is carried inside the variant's own stream. The playlist parser
# keeps such a rendition, as the successor's parser does (setup_streams and the playlist update
# already skip one as "a placeholder for a stream contained in another mux"), and its tags go out
# on the variant's stream in a sticky "hls-rendition-tags" event holding one tag list per stream
# type, for the demuxer splitting that stream to apply to its streams of that type (see the
# tsdemux and qtdemux patches).
#
# A subtitle rendition otherwise travels the path the audio renditions already take: its
# fragments are typefound (WebVTT types as application/x-subtitle-vtt) and pushed as their own
# stream, and is_primary_playlist stays false for every rendition, so bitrate switching keeps
# following the main playlist.
#
# A rendition without a URI marked DEFAULT sets "<type>-default" in the hls-rendition-tags event,
# so the demuxer splitting the variant's stream selects its stream of that type. A subtitle
# rendition with FORCED=YES carries the characteristic "public.subtitles.forced-only", the value
# of AVFoundation's AVMediaCharacteristicContainsOnlyForcedSubtitles. When setup_streams reuses the
# streams of the previous variant it skips a rendition without a URI, as stream creation and the
# playlist update already do.
#
# Applied by build_deps with patch -p1.
